</div></div></div><div class="col sqs-col-6 span-6"><div class="row sqs-row"><div class="col sqs-col-1 span-1"><div class="sqs-block website-component-block sqs-block-website-component sqs-block-spacer spacer-block sized vsize-1" data-block-css="[&quot;https://definitions.sqspcdn.com/website-component-definition/static-assets/website.components.spacer/431d1633-0cbe-49e3-8e36-f1320ea12e05_1352/website.components.spacer.styles.css&quot;]" data-block-scripts="[&quot;https://definitions.sqspcdn.com/website-component-definition/static-assets/website.components.spacer/431d1633-0cbe-49e3-8e36-f1320ea12e05_1352/website.components.spacer.visitor.js&quot;]" data-block-type="1337" data-definition-name="website.components.spacer" data-website-component-id="8ff623bc8a87424dac34" id="block-8ff623bc8a87424dac34"><div class="sqs-block-content">&nbsp;</div></div></div><div class="col sqs-col-5 span-5"><div class="sqs-block website-component-block sqs-block-website-component sqs-block-html html-block" data-block-css="[&quot;https://definitions.sqspcdn.com/website-component-definition/static-assets/website.components.html/b481d24d-7cfe-4ac4-8f20-65b926413244_1029/website.components.html.styles.css&quot;]" data-block-scripts="[&quot;https://definitions.sqspcdn.com/website-component-definition/static-assets/website.components.html/b481d24d-7cfe-4ac4-8f20-65b926413244_1029/website.components.html.visitor.js&quot;]" data-block-type="1337" data-definition-name="website.components.html" data-sqsp-block="text" data-website-component-id="6afde25f9686c281bd9d" id="block-6afde25f9686c281bd9d"><div class="sqs-block-content"><div class="sqs-text-block-container">
  
  <div class="sqs-html-content" data-sqsp-text-block-content><p class="sqsrte-small" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The history of conservation districts begins with the Dust Bowl. As settlers moved out west, agriculture boomed, especially as demand for wheat corn, and other row crops rose in the late 1800’s and into the early 1900’s. Over decades, farmers stripped the Southern Plains of native grasses and over plowed the bare land. Years of drought and strong winds in the 1930’s removed nearly 100 million acres of loose, nutrient-rich topsoil, blowing it thousands of miles away. Without topsoil, the agricultural land was lost.&nbsp;</p><p class="sqsrte-small" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">After the Dust Bowl, President Franklin D. Roosevelt ordered the creation of Conservation Districts in every state and county across the US to teach farmers, landowners, and the general public how to protect the soil, water, and air.&nbsp;</p></div>


  
